  "geometryEquivalence": "The synthetic target is fixed one million metres along the ground station geodetic zenith. Its observer-to-target direction is therefore exactly the zenith. Angular separation from the observer-to-Sun direction is pi/2 minus solar elevation. SUN_EXCLUSION >=96 degrees therefore exactly reproduces the published civil-night condition solar elevation<=-6 degrees, with no refraction. This is a test of SUN_EXCLUSION; no generic ground-night constraint is claimed.",
